Track 3: The Ghost of Accra-San Juan
- Story & Context: Decades after the generation ship lost contact with ground controllers, this track survived as a legendary folklore anthem played at every deep-space funeral on the ship's outer rim. Built around a ghost-like sample of an unknown 1970s Ghanaian Highlife record stretched until the brass notes sound like dying stars, the track merges endless layers of weeping synth strings with a slow, pounding sub-bass drop that mimics a dying ship heart. Legend says the final verse was recorded by an anonymous rapper who walked out into the airlock wearing no helmet, leaving only his voice echoed through the comms stream. "San Juan está muy lejos y Accra se nos borró" ("San Juan is too far away and Accra has been erased from us").
